The \emph{Bethe-Bloch} formula provides the average energy loss per unit distance:
\begin{align}
-\expval{\dv{E}{x}} = K z^2 \frac{Z}{A} \frac{1}{\beta^{2}}.
\end{align}
At low particle energies, the $1/\beta^2$ term dominates.
